.
.TH str2s 3 (date) liba2i-(unreleased)
.
.
.SH Name
str2s,
str2shh,
str2sh,
str2si,
str2sl,
str2sll,
\-
convert a string to a signed integer
.
.
.SH Library
String-to-integer library
.RI ( liba2i ", " \-la2i )
.
.
.SH Synopsis
.nf
.B #include <a2i/str2i/str2s.h>
.fi
.
.P
.B int
.SY str2s (
.B TYPE,
.BI TYPE\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS
.
.P
.B int
.SY str2shh (
.BI signed\~char\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS .
.B int
.SY str2sh (
.BI short\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS .
.B int
.SY str2si (
.BI int\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS .
.B int
.SY str2sl (
.BI long\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS .
.B int
.SY str2sll (
.BI long\~long\~*restrict\~ n ,
.BI const\~char\~* s );
.YS .
.
.SH Description
These functions and macro
are convenience wrappers around
.BR a2s (3),
providing common defaults for the remaining arguments.
The base is 0;
the end pointer is NULL;
and the limits are those of the type.
.
.
.SH Examples
The following calls are all equivalent:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
str2sl(&n, s);
str2s(long, &n, s);
str2i(long, &n, s);
a2sl(&n, s, NULL, 0, LONG_MIN, LONG_MAX);
a2s(long, &n, s, NULL, 0, LONG_MIN, LONG_MAX);
a2i(long, &n, s, NULL, 0, LONG_MIN, LONG_MAX);
.EE
.in
.
.
.SH See also
.BR a2i (3),
.BR a2s (3),
.BR a2u (3),
.BR str2i (3),
.BR str2u (3)
